l":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/labels/accepted","name":"accepted","color":"0052cc","default":false,"description":"There is consensus among the team that this change meets the criteria for inclusion"},{"id":829215248,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw4MjkyMTUyNDg=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/labels/archived%20due%20to%20age","name":"archived due to age","color":"eeeeee","default":false,"description":"This issue has been archived; please open a new issue for any further discussion"}],"state":"closed","locked":true,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2015-07-07T07:17:34Z","updated_at":"2018-02-07T00:56:40Z","closed_at":"2015-07-07T18:19:06Z","author_association":"MEMBER","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"I tried to write a jsdoc comment for a field, but the comment seems to be bonded to a function in its right hand expression.\n\nOn the following code, I expected the comment `\"Description for this.xs\"` is bonded to `this.xs`, but actually the comment seems to be bonded to `x => x != null`.\n\n``` js\n/**\n * Description for A.\n */\nclass A {\n  /**\n   * Description for constructor.\n   * @param {object[]} xs - xs\n   */\n  constructor(xs) {\n    /**\n     * Description for this.xs;\n     * @type {object[]}\n     */\n    this.xs = xs.filter(x => x != null);\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n```\n> eslint -v\nv0.24.0\n> eslint test.js --env es6 --rule \"valid-jsdoc:[2,{requireReturn:false}]\" --reset --no-eslintrc\n```\n## Actual\n\n```\ntest.js\n  10:4  error  Missing JSDoc for parameter 'x'  valid-jsdoc\n\n✖ 1 problem (1 error, 0 warnings)\n```\n## Expected\n\nNo errors.\n","closed_by":{"login":"gyandeeps","id":5554486,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NTQ0ODY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5554486?v=4","gravatar_id":"",